From 547a9f796d5e96e12e7bb566307c0577481338a8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: UMP <ump@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/90] java mods: animate mods' mobs (client twins, walk
 animation)

Mods animate their mobs on the client: Naturalist starts its walk/run/idle AnimationStates in tick() only when level.isClientSide(), and LivingEntity.aiStep steps the limb swing only on a client level. Mods' mobs lived on the mirror's server level alone, so they were drawn in their standing pose while moving.

Each mod mob now gets a twin in the mirror's client level: the server mob's place, facing, motion and synced data are copied in each tick (what a client gets from packets), the twin ticks as a client entity, and the renderer draws the twin. Types whose twin fails fall back to the server mob (logged once). HORIZON_JAVA_CLIENT_TWINS=0 turns it off. Also steps calculateEntityAnimation for every mod mob, and HORIZON_JAVA_DEBUG=poses logs model part rotations (UMP's animation test).

Measured with UMP's anim test on 66 mod mobs (Friends & Foes, Mutant Monsters, Naturalist): animating 7 -> 62, frozen 47 -> 0.
